    "details": "<p><strong>Overview</strong></p>\n<p>Have an idea that could solve a real-world problem? Bring it to <strong>IDEATHON 2026</strong>, organised by the <strong>AICTE IDEA Lab, New Horizon College of Engineering (NHCE), Bengaluru</strong>.</p>\n<p>IDEATHON 2026 brings together students to explore challenges, exchange ideas, and develop innovative solutions. It is an opportunity to apply your knowledge, think creatively, and collaborate with fellow participants who share your interest in innovation.</p>\n<p><strong>Registration and Guidelines</strong></p>\n<p>Before registering, participants should:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Carefully read the Rulebook</strong>, which contains the necessary instructions, guidelines, and participation requirements.</li>\n<li><strong>️*Complete registration as instructed on the website. Note if failing to register in offical website the registration cannot be consdidered*</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Offical Site : </strong><strong><a href=\"https://newhorizoncollegeofengineering.in/ideathon/\">Ideathon 2026 &mdash; AICTE IDEA LAB @ NHCE</a></strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Please refer to the official portal and Rulebook for complete event details and requirements.</p>\n<p><strong>Event Details</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Event:</strong> IDEATHON 2026</li>\n<li><strong>Organiser:</strong> AICTE IDEA Lab, New Horizon College of Engineering</li>\n<li><strong>Dates:</strong> 3rd, 4th, and 5th November 2026</li>\n<li><strong>Venue:</strong> New Horizon College of Engineering, Bengaluru</li>\n<li><strong>Participation Mode:</strong> Offline; a hybrid option can be provided to participants outside Karnataka if requested.</li>\n<li><strong>Registration Status:</strong> Registrations are now open</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Bring your ideas, challenge your creativity, and take a step towards solving real-world problems. Register now for IDEATHON 2026!</strong></p>\n<p>Organised by AICTE IDEA Lab, New Horizon College of Engineering (NHCE), Bengaluru.</p>",
